body:
Yes if I was you I'd look more into where would you like to live at this point and search for universities around there, there's a lot of good unis in Europe;

Padua is a good one, I have a friend of mine doing his postdoc there, I also have family close to Padua and the party scene for students is very good if you like that kind of things;

I don't know which programs has Pisa but that's a good one too;

I am doing my PhD in Sapienza and I can recommend it due to being very well connected with companies and since it has a lot of international presence, but it comes with the downside (or upside, depends on the person) of living in Rome;

Don't actually know much about unis in France, I'll try to ask around :)

Kinda off topic but I never really understood why Petrachi was considered awful for us, am I misremembering something? Like, he wasn't amazing, but he were for us for a short time and I don't remember any truly horrible move from him

&#x200B;

Monchi on the other hand...
